module Core

### Represents the aggregate protocol for `crashable`-kind error types — the value-category marker
### `throw` produces and `Check[T]`/`Lookup[T]` transport. Like `RecordType`/`VariantType`, it bundles
### NO method requirements: `crash_message`/`crash_title` are buildtime-GUARANTEED on every crashable by
### the `needs CrashableType T` derives in `Derivation.rf` (a type may `@override` either), exactly as
### `represent`/`diagnose` are universal built-ins rather than opt-in protocol methods. Conformance is the
### `crashable` KIND (`TypeCategory.Crashable`), not a structural member check.
protocol Crashable
  pass
